{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/323473-shan-iatu-and-gilgamesh-spoilers","id":323473,"title":"Shan'iatu and Gilgamesh : Spoilers!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-27T00:28:05-08:00","id":323473,"title":"Shan'iatu and Gilgamesh : Spoilers!","content":"... reading between the lines of Book of the Deceived, it really seems like that the narrator is claiming the Shan'iatu sacrificed Gilgamesh to Ammut to get her to speak again. They reference the empire of 'Ki-En-Gir' which is Akkadian for for 'Sumer'. They also reference a sorcerer king who is one third divine, where as in the famous epic the same claim is made of Gilgamesh. Neat, huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T02:07:36-08:00","id":323533,"title":"","content":"Gilgamesh is a Hero (ala Beast) in my head cannon.<br /> <br /> Which will make this interesting when I have all pieces to try and do a write up. But a few Sebu attached to his soul would be a good start. Thanks for pointing it out, I missed it before","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 11-07-2019, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:42:21-08:00","id":323625,"title":"","content":"I didn't catch that in my first read through.<br /> <br /> That's hysterical, except the corebook claim the Ki-En-Gir were from Canaan, not Sumer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T10:02:50-08:00","id":323722,"title":"","content":"Canaan actually is more or less the area where Sumer was located, so that actually conforms to the hypothesis as well!<br /> <br /> So from this we can conclude 'Ubar' was a city that the Sumerians built, and that the empire of Ubar is in fact Sumerian. Gilgamesh was the sorcerer-king. The city Gilgamesh helped build and oversee was called 'Uruk' in Sumerian mythology. Uruk had a number of very impressive ziggurats, any one of which could have been the ancient citadel where the barrier between worlds grows threadbare.<br /> <br /> This is pretty cool because we even know where Uruk is in the modern day, so now if you use google earth, you should be able to more or less tell where this epic battle took place...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tools.wmflabs.org/geohack/geohack.php?pagename=Uruk&amp;params=31_19_20_N_45_38_10_E_type:landmark\" target=\"_blank\">31\u00b019\u203220\u2033N 45\u00b038\u203210\u2033E</a><br /> <br /> My previous research to establish the location of Irem would indicate that the Iremites marched north to engage Ubar! Almost 800 miles.<br /> <br /> I'm curious though, why does Mummy go to such great lengths to file the serial numbers off of this stuff? It's really fascinating. Whoever wrote this went to a lot of trouble to match this up with some historical easter eggs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T10:36:26-08:00","id":323738,"title":"","content":"Do the dates line up properly?<br /> <br /> I don't think Gilgamesh was actually the king of Uruk at the time that the Nameless Empire was conquering that region, because the Rite of Return took place around 3832 BCE and that was well after the conquest of the Ki-En-Gar. Furthermore, Gilgamesh's dates are somewhere between 2800 and 2500 BCE,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T12:11:43-08:00","id":323811,"title":"","content":"Gilgamesh is sort of a hard figure to place. We don't really have any evidence of when he ruled except for OTHER figures we can date that appear in the Epic - and the most of the epic was written more than a thousand years after the events depicted. Over time, it's common with legends of this nature for less important supporting characters and nations to be 'updated' with more modern placeholders that are more relatable which makes this method of indirect dating difficult; this happens a lot in the Bible, for example. So while some informed opinions exist as to his timeline, scholars don't really regard those dates as definitive (not at all surprising given this was a really, really long time ago), enough flex room exists to accommodate Mummy.<br /> <br /> If one accepts those figures as genuine though? Yep, timeline issues do exist - despite this, I think specifically naming Ubar as Sumer (in Akkadian) and a citing a sorcerer king who is one third divine are pretty good hints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T23:45:53-08:00","id":324246,"title":"","content":"This is so badass I don't care if the timelines match up. &quot;Memory makes it not make sense&quot; is good enough for me.<br /> (Time is a diamond anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}